  "description": "Roslyn analyzers that enforce the shape of types based on what they inherit or implement, configured in .editorconfig: for example, every IEndpoint implementation must be internal and sealed, every request handler must have its own IFooHandler interface, entities must not expose public setters or mutable collections or hold other aggregate roots, value objects must be immutable, compare by value and be created through factory methods, and EF Core configurations must live in a Database.Configurations namespace. Violations show up in the IDE while you type, and fail the build with TreatWarningsAsErrors, instead of waiting for an architecture test to run. Most rules have a code fix, offered only when applying it can't break the build.",
